      "claim": "Fluconazole passes into breast milk in small amounts. These amounts are estimated to be less than the dose that could be given directly to an infant to treat an infection. Taking a single dose of fluconazole while breastfeeding is unlikely to cause problems for the breastfed infant. If you suspect the baby has any symptoms, such as stomach upset or diarrhea, contact the child’s healthcare provider.",
